Organisational ancestry and political tendency are separate. SLD/Nowa Lewica,
Wiosna, Razem and PPS are organisations; labour, feminist, progressive,
social-patriot and market currents can cross those formal lines. An affinity
estimate is not a seat transfer: only completed defections alter the chamber
charts.

- @menu: Back to index

@institutions
title: Constitutional institutions
go-to: menu

= Constitutional institutions

Poland is a parliamentary republic with a directly elected president and a
bicameral legislature. The President signs, vetoes or refers legislation,
appoints a prime-ministerial candidate in the first formation step and
represents the state, but does not direct routine cabinet policy.

The Sejm grants confidence to the Council of Ministers. A constructive vote of
no confidence must name a replacement prime minister and assemble **231
deputies**. The Senate does not participate in confidence votes.

The courts, prosecution service, National Council of the Judiciary and
Constitutional Tribunal retain separate legitimacy and appointment records.
Political control of one office never silently resolves the authority of the
others.

